  "full_text": "So in school I was often the top student and people kind of hated me and it's kind of interesting. The Bible says something about the excellence of Jacob being like a bad thing and it's kind of a certain pig aspect like if you hog the glory then Maybe you think you're really awesome, but you've actually turned people wicked. So if you see somebody who's wicked, it might be because you stole the grace or the goodness or something. In other words, maybe if you hadn't have been so excellent, they wouldn't have turned out wicked because you stole their glory. Maybe you stole their endorphins. If you see somebody wicked, maybe it's your own fault because you were too good or something. Just think about the student, right? Like the head student is like, I don't know why these other people hate me because they're not as good. And you've created wickedness, you know. Interesting thought. I was thinking about grace and big and small. I won't go out on a limb. Won't put myself in jeopardy for other people very often. I'm kind of I'm not I'm not really like I Don't know not intentionally if I get stuck with it. I just deal with it I'm pretty good about just accepting what I got I guess I don't know if that's good, but uh if you're a good person and You're good about it. Just accepting what you got and that's kind of grace that you were a good person You know in some respects then there's big people who? pass grace forward, something like that. If you put yourself out for others, then you're creating grace. So there's a certain question of my debt. If I receive grace, there's kind of a question like, do I have to pass grace forward by being a big person or something like that? But anyway...",
